// wdoc section: Math Equations.
page wdoc_math { sites = [:reference]
  h1 "Math Equations"

  p "`math` typesets a LaTeX equation to inline SVG via the pure-Rust RaTeX toolchain. Glyph outlines embed in the SVG, so equations render the same whether the page is opened locally or served over HTTP — no webfont dependency."

  h2 "Block equations"

  p "`math \"…\" {}` (or `math <<TEX … TEX`) renders a centred display equation. Use a raw heredoc for backslash-heavy LaTeX. Previewed in a card:"

  diagram { width = 460  height = 140
    card { x = 16.0  y = 12.0  width = 428.0  height = 116.0
      math "E = mc^2"
      math <<'TEX'
\frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}
TEX
    }
  }

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
math "E = mc^2"

math <<'TEX'
\frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}
TEX
WCL
  }

  p "Its fields:"

  type_table { type = Math }

  h2 "Inline math"

  p "Inside any `p` body or `span`, two inline patterns produce math. Live: the mass-energy relation $E = mc^2$ flows with this sentence, and the display form $$\\int_0^1 x^2 \\, dx$$ sits a touch larger on the same line."

  code wcl {
    source = <<'PATTERNS'
$x^2$           // → inline LaTeX (text style — flows with the prose)
$$\int x dx$$   // → display style (slightly bigger, same line)
PATTERNS
  }

  table {
    rows:
      | "Pattern" | "Style" |
      | "`$…$`"   | "Text-style inline math — flows with the surrounding prose." |
      | "`$$…$$`" | "Display-style inline math — slightly larger, still inline." |
  }

  p "The `$…$` pattern requires a non-space at each delimiter, so currency like `$10 or $20` is left alone."

  p "Next: [Tables](wdoc_tables)."
}
